From c7ff00c05d4349567f9b5c558d3854cad745c1fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:57:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: stranded-park review fixes

- B1: an open kernel recovery card (open_recovery_card) or a judged goal hold
  (current_park) owns the park; re-kinding it would make the recovery resume
  refuse with human_gate and the requester skip it.
- B2: a triage card the stale-triage sweep will still release (entry newer than
  its last triage_swept, not capped, not gate-held, not a spend/containment
  hold) is agent-owned; the predicate is shared with sweep_stale_triage
  (kanban_triage_sweep._PENDING / awaiting_stale_sweep).
- B3: the generated ask has no choices (default Unblock/Archive buttons answer
  it) and follows the ask-line convention; a spend-pending card's unblock names
  `hermes kanban promote <id> --reason ...` (new spend window).
- S1: lane-gate holds and shared-blocker parks (payload.blocker_id) are skipped.
- S2: the desk subscription is written inside the escalation txn, after the
  re-check and before the event.

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
